==English==
===Etymology 1===
{{wikipedia}}
Height of [[w:Oliver R. Smoot|Oliver R. Smoot]], who lay on the Harvard Bridge to measure it as an MIT fraternity prank.

====Pronunciation====
* {{enPR|smo͞ot}}
* {{IPA|/smuːt/|lang=en}}

====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# {{context|chiefly|Greater Boston|lang=en}} A [[unit]] of [[length]] defined as exactly sixty-seven [[inch|inches]] (approximately 1.70 [[meter|meters]]).

===Etymology 2===

====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# {{context|British|lang=en}} A small opening built into a [[dry-stone]] wall as a [[bolthole]] allowing a person to cross the wall while impeding the livestock.

